#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1321 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "FRESH, DISCRIMINATING (multiplicity of the SUPPAE-absent fire - the twin pins it only with ONE subject). No SUPPAE block at all: the broadcast disjunct is TRUE on every row and the grouped count is 0 for every subject; emission is per USUBJID group -> predict TWO Group findings. ESCALATE if it reports 1 (a broadcast-fold collapse to a dataset-level finding would be a real discovery)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEDECOD type=Char label="Dictionary-Derived Term"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | Headache | HEADACHE
S1 | AE | 002 | 1 | Nausea   | NAUSEA
